{"ready":true,"data":{"id":"sam-neill","name":"Sam Neill","birthDate":"1947-09-14","birthPlace":"Omagh, County Tyrone, Northern Ireland, UK","bio":"Sir Nigel John Dermot 'Sam' Neill (September 14, 1947 – July 13, 2026) was a New Zealand actor. His career included leading roles in both dramas and blockbusters. Considered an 'international leading man', he is regarded as one of the most versatile actors of his generation.\n\nBorn in Northern Ireland to an English mother and New Zealand father, Neill moved to Christchurch with his family in 1954. He first achieved recognition with his appearance in the film Sleeping Dogs (1977), which he followed with leading roles in My Brilliant Career (1979), Omen III: The Final Conflict, Possession (both 1981), Evil Angels (1988), Dead Calm (1989), The Hunt for Red October (1990), The Piano (1993), and In the Mouth of Madness (1994). He came to international prominence as Dr. Alan Grant in Jurassic Park (1993), reprising the role in Jurassic Park III (2001) and Dominion (2022).\n\nOutside of film, Neill appeared in numerous television series in guest and recurring roles, including Reilly, Ace of Spies (1983), The Simpsons (1994), The Tudors (2007), Crusoe (2008–2010), Happy Town (2010), Alcatraz (2012), and Rick and Morty (2019). He also starred as the titular character in Merlin (1998) and Merlin's Apprentice (2006), and as Major Chester Campbell in the first two series of Peaky Blinders (2013–2014). He has presented and narrated several documentaries.\n\nNeill received the AACTA Award for Best Actor in a Leading Role, the Longford Lyell Award, the New Zealand Film Award, and the Logie Award for Most Outstanding Actor. He also had three Golden Globe and two Primetime Emmy nominations. He won the Silver Logie for Most Popular Actor at the 2023 Logies.\n\nNeill passed away at age 78 on 13 July 2026, in Sydney, Australia. The loss was sudden and unexpected but blessed by the fact that he remained cancer free.\n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Sam Neill, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia.","source":"TMDB","fetchedAt":"2026-11-19T17:44:43+00:00","tmdbId":4783,"sourceUrl":"https://www.themoviedb.org/person/4783","credits":[{"id":"thor-ragnarok","title":"Thor: Ragnarok","character":"Actor Odin","characterFa":"بازیگر اودین"},{"id":"thor-love","title":"Thor: Love and Thunder","character":"Actor Odin","characterFa":"بازیگر اودین"}],"photo":"./public-data/images/people/sam-neill.webp","filmography":[{"name":"Godzilla x Kong: Supernova","year":2027,"character":"","mediaType":"movie","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/gEGDDG6QMDFZ1sV32CGxvzaVPnv.jpg"},{"name":"The Last Resort","year":2027,"character":"Gerard","mediaType":"movie","poster":""},{"name":"The Legend of Zelda","year":2027,"character":"","mediaType":"movie","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/4XuaHHQ5eR9czPZPHcaaUjekx5w.jpg"},{"name":"The Fox","year":2026,"character":"The Magpie (voice)","mediaType":"movie","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/unIaSB9LZ0r3iZ2jBAQ2Qi5mFIp.jpg"},{"name":"Dinosaur Drive-In","year":2026,"character":"Self - (archive footage)","mediaType":"movie","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/o1HDtezAKVeSxpOOOCYyroiUSvJ.jpg"},{"name":"Not Only Fred Dagg But Also John Clarke","year":2025,"character":"Self","mediaType":"movie","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/dK4rNebxs5ZguMUF6eZPj8umDA.jpg"},{"name":"UNTAMED","year":2025,"character":"Paul Souter","mediaType":"tv","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/tclYY8RGieQwkJXDxZGf505Zybr.jpg"},{"name":"T. REX","year":2024,"character":"Self - Narrator (voice)","mediaType":"movie","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/q7GF5Vov2fl7U8rfGLm7rk5aq2C.jpg"},{"name":"Apples Never Fall","year":2024,"character":"Stan Delaney","mediaType":"tv","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/goa4saZkf8r4zmBNgS6IiiPxEEN.jpg"},{"name":"The Assembly","year":2024,"character":"Self","mediaType":"tv","poster":"https://image.tmdb.o